MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I am trying to process a huge tree, whereby I want to get a printout list/vector/df of a designated clade's tip labels that occur after a selected node, so I can use that list of taxa in each clade to subset other data, rather then having to type out a ton of tip labels in each clade.

I can subset the tree and identify specific clades with subset_tree, or groupClade, and get a visual of these groupings, but have been unable to figure out how to get a list. I see the groupings are stored in the tree object as attributes, but I haven't been successful at accessing them.

Any help would be great!

Thanks,
Kurt

